Cell["\<\
N[Binomial[2j,j]] alone does not overflow in Mathematica (exact integer \
converted with an extended exponent range). The actual failure mode of the \
direct formula is (i) individual xi^(j-m) terms hitting genuine machine \
underflow/overflow once th,ph are literal machine numbers (General::munfl \
fires already at j=2000), and (ii) forming (2j)!-scale exact Binomial \
coefficients over the full range becomes computationally expensive. Directly \
timed at j=8192 (this notebook's actual target): SCSStable and SCSKrylov both \
complete, agree to ~1e-12, and normalize to 1; the direct/exact route was \
impractically slow at that size in this kernel. Use SCSStable or SCSKrylov, \
not SCSExact, from here on for j at or above a few hundred.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2bf4e161-7895-694d-91bc-6daa3d712b3c"],

Cell["\<\
Note on core_QKT.m: that file runs the kick on Jx^2 with the free rotation \
diagonal on Jz -- the mirror image of both papers' Jz^2-kick / Jx-free \
convention. This is a valid unitarily-equivalent relabeling (its parity \
generator is Rz, diagonal by construction, not Rx), not an error, but it is a \
different convention from the one built here, which follows the papers' \
Jz^2/Jx/Rx form directly for a 1:1 correspondence with their equations.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1f58eb30-63b2-d04d-b50a-d9bc1a999ebb"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
